00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:32.140
So, or less, who knows what the, what the time dilation is there.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:43.020
And the opening of this game has extreme polish in a way that probably sets the rest of the game up for failure because, uh, you know, let's just start with the intro.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:47.200
It has this awesome theme, feels kind of like the Superman, uh, theme song.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:54.540
This intro cinematic where it gives you all, you know, starring Rick Stalker and all these other people and great graphics.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:07:09.440
You get into the actual game and there's this tutorial with an NES controller on the screen with a clear explanation of the fighting mechanics and showing you like these red diamonds where this is like, this is that person's weak spot.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.580
And when this thing appears on screen, you should press these buttons.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:17.400
And it's like, wow, this is, this is a heavy level of detail to get into the game.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.880
