00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:58.780
And it's basically, you've got all these pages, again, of how to fight in this game.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:06.260
And it's about, like, you know, if you want to punch towards their head, towards their chest, towards their feet,

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.020
or if you want to kick, yada, yada.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.540
How do you block high and low?

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:18.240
If you play the difficulty of the game that Mike and I played, it's literally just two buttons,

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:22.620
and they keep telling you how to block things the same way over and over.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:33.160
However, it's pretty comical when you look at it that way, that you kind of just kneecapped all of the complexity of the game.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:39.920
But I do have to say that I'm glad that they put it in there, because I feel like this would be a huge source of frustration otherwise.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:41.520
Yeah, it's true.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:48.320
And even beyond just, like, the differences of punch and kick and stuff like that,

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:59.740
there are, like, you know, fighting game style button combinations that you have to do with some of the more, like, special skills in the game.

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:05.620
And so there's no, like, there's no quarter swing or whatever, whatever that is on the D-pad,

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.500
where you do, like, a half quarter or whatever.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.300
Right. There's none of that.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:12.620
But it still is impressive that we're getting, like, this close.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:16.980
It's almost like, you know, because this is Culture Brain, who is the developer of this game.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.660
So it's not like they're, like, cheating with Capcom on the homework or whatever.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.600
